[
  {
    "id": "hld_tree_json",
    "title": "High-Level Design in Tree JSON Format",
    "description": "Generate HLD for any system in a nested JSON structure.",
    "prompt": "Generate a High-Level Design (HLD) for a [system name or type of application], in a tree-like JSON format. The root node should be the system name, and each child node should represent a major component (e.g., Frontend, Backend, Database, Services, Storage, DevOps, Security). Each component may have nested children representing subcomponents, services, or modules.\n\nFollow this exact structure:\n{\n  \"name\": \"System Name\",\n  \"children\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Component\",\n      \"children\": [\n        { \"name\": \"Subcomponent\" },\n        ...\n      ]\n    },\n    ...\n  ]\n}\n\nEnsure the output is valid JSON. No explanation, only the JSON structure."
  }
]



